Z||000000||fieroshop||10-02-1999||11:00 PM||||I've had to work on a lot of Fieros. Especially working on Fieros all day long every day up to 7 days a week. But being in the San Francisco Bay Area we don't get too many Fieros from the East coast. Until now that is, I've been trying to repair an 87 GT that came here from New Jersey and talk about rust. Every time I touch a bolt it breaks off or I have to use the torch on it. Is this a normal phenomana back east or is this a special case. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||lews84||10-03-1999||12:19 AM||||I just removed the Torques (sp?) screws that hold the side marker lights and the clips that the screws went into just disintigrated.<BR>This is a NY and CT car.<P>Then I figured out that you can replace the bulb without pulling the whole assembly, just reach up underneath, un'screw' the socket and there's the bulb. <P>Now I have to replace 2 clips. Do I feel dumb.<p>[This message has been edited by lews84 (edited 10-03-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||10-03-1999||02:15 AM||||Get a 55gal. drum of that special re-move-all spray (AKA WD40)???<P>Glad to see you found time to join in on the fourm Fieroshop. 7 days a week of fiero fun, I wish I could do that. You know, "so much to do, so little time". Man you sure are lucky!!!||||reg||10
Z||000003||fastonpumpgas||10-03-1999||02:28 AM||||I live in ohio and I have barely any rust, I alittle on the battery tray, and the headbolts of coarse . but that is good I think for a 15 year old car||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||10-03-1999||07:44 AM||||I live on the Cape in Mass. and rust is a big issue out here. We get plenty of salt in the air all summer and on the ground in the winter. Last week I just got done going over the whole underbody using Extend rust destroyer in the spots needed then used 4 cans of rubberized undercoating. It's a battle I plan on winning!||||reg||8
Z||000005||fieroshop||10-03-1999||10:39 AM||||Hey dxr_dad, I am having a lot of fun working on Fieros and seeing Fieros come in on the hook or in bad disrepair. But when they leave here with new engines or new paint it makes me feel good. Unfortunatly for the owner of this Fiero from New Jersey which he bought off the internet and went flew back east to pickup and drove it here. All he wanted was to be able to drive and enjoy the car but we are having to almost rebuild have of it, this is so that he can pass smog and safety||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||10-03-1999||06:19 PM||||depends on just where in NJ it came from...... If it was near the coast I'm not suprised it's crapped up.....<P>NJ and DE winter salt use varies. MD doesn't use it at all as far as I know. PA, NY, and north can use quite allot.<P>People who know how to deal with this wash the bottoms of their cars regularly... people who don't get the kind of mess you have. I've even seen some smart people near the coast use marine grade hardware to at least reduce many rusted bolts. ||||reg||1
